            <ArticleTitle>Dorsal pancreatic agenesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>450-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="CONTEXT" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Agenesis of the dorsal pancreas is a rare entity and might present with various symptoms. We report a case which presented with chronic pancreatitis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">The patient presented with epigastric pain and we found dorsal pancreatic agenesis causing chronic pancreatitis.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Dorsal pancreatic agenesis can be easily diagnosed with new techniques and its association with clinical syndromes can be better understood.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
